2026-11-06T15:31:05.4739856Z If <cleanup code> does not mention `err` or perform `return`/`break`/`continue`, rewrite to:
2026-11-06T15:31:05.4740176Z 
2026-11-06T15:31:05.4740267Z   errdefer <cleanup code>
2026-11-06T15:31:05.4740697Z   <expr>
2026-11-06T15:31:05.4740796Z 
2026-11-06T15:31:05.4741256Z Note: `try ... catch` will no longer capture async cancellation in the future, so using `catch` for cleanup is dangerous for async code.
2026-11-06T15:31:05.4741989Z If your handler need to manipulate or inspect `err`, but contain cleanup code as well,
2026-11-06T15:31:05.4742665Z it is still recommended to move the cleanup part to `errdefer` as well, leaving only the error inspecting part in `catch`.
